1. Iris Dataset
Scikit-learn built-in
Used in: Experiments 1, 2, 7 and 8.

Contains 150 flower samples from three Iris species: setosa, versicolor and virginica.
- Features: sepal length, sepal width, petal length and petal width.
- Target: flower species (3 classes).
- Purpose: descriptive statistics, DataFrame operations, KNN classification and entropy-based decision trees.
- Loader: load_iris()












2. Diabetes Dataset
Scikit-learn built-in
Used in: Experiments 3 and 4.

Contains 442 samples with baseline medical measurements and a quantitative measure of disease progression.
- Features: age, sex, BMI, blood pressure and six blood-serum measurements.
- Target: quantitative disease-progression measure.
- Features used in our programs: BMI only.
- Purpose: linear regression, polynomial regression and MSE evaluation.
- Loader: load_diabetes()












3. Breast Cancer Wisconsin Dataset
Scikit-learn built-in
Used in: Experiment 5.

Contains 569 samples of breast-mass measurements, with 30 numerical features computed from digitized images of fine-needle aspirates.
- Features: radius, texture, perimeter, area, smoothness and other cell-nucleus characteristics.
- Target: malignant or benign (2 classes).
- Purpose: Logistic Regression and classification accuracy.
- Loader: load_breast_cancer()












4. Wine Recognition Dataset
Scikit-learn built-in
Used in: Experiments 6 and 9.

Contains 178 wine samples described by chemical measurements and grouped into three wine cultivars.
- Features: alcohol, malic acid, ash, magnesium, flavanoids, color intensity and other chemical properties.
- Target: one of 3 wine classes.
- Purpose: Gaussian Naive Bayes and CART decision tree classification.
- Loader: load_wine()












5. Logic-Gate Truth Tables
Mathematical examples
Used in: Experiment 10.

These are not a built-in Scikit-learn dataset. They contain all four possible combinations of two binary inputs.
- Features: two inputs, each either 0 or 1.
- Targets: AND, OR and XOR outputs.
- Purpose: train and test a neural network on logical relationships.



